   169	## 3. THEOREM SMOOTH-KILL — `A_F` is singular at every degree
   170	
   171	REP-96 §7 (R4) runs the nodal collapse at `N = 4` in the two branches `a = 2`
   172	and `a = 1`, and the `a = 1` branch is refuted "for every `s >= 1`". The
   173	boundary case `s = 0` is therefore *not* covered: a nodal curve with no nodes is
   174	a smooth curve, and `(M')` is **satisfied** there. This is the first thing a
   175	general-`N` treatment has to close, and it closes completely.
   176	
   177	> **THEOREM SMOOTH-KILL.** Let `F` be a noninvertible plane Keller map with
   178	> `A_F` irreducible. Then `A_F` is **singular**: `s >= 1`.
   179	>
   180	> *Proof.* Suppose `s = 0`. Then `nu = 0` and `D = D_0` is smooth, irreducible,
   181	> with `D~ ≅ A^1` (Lemma A); a smooth curve equals its normalization, so
   182	> `D ≅ A^1` and `chi_c(D) = 1`.
   183	>
   184	> (a) *`a = 1`.* Lemma 3.3 makes `E := F^{-1}(D) -> D` a covering of degree `a`,
   185	> so `chi_c(E) = a·chi_c(D) = a`. Theorem (E) gives
   186	> `1 = N(1 - chi_c(D)) + chi_c(E) = N·0 + a`. Hence `a = 1`.
   187	>
   188	> (b) *Both curves are coordinate lines.* `D ⊂ A^2` is closed and isomorphic to
   189	> `A^1`, so by **Abhyankar–Moh–Suzuki** there is `α ∈ Aut(A^2)` with
   190	> `α(D) = {v = 0}`. Replace `F` by `α ∘ F`: still Keller, still noninvertible,
   191	> and `A_{α∘F} = α(A_F) = {v = 0}`. Now `a = 1` makes `E -> D` an étale map of
   192	> degree one, i.e. an isomorphism, so `E ≅ A^1`; `E` is closed in `A^2`, so AMS
   193	> again gives `β ∈ Aut(A^2)` with `β^{-1}(E) = {x = 0}`. Replace `F` by `F ∘ β`.
   194	>
   195	> (c) *Contradiction.* `D = {v = 0}` has reduced equation `h = v`, so
   196	> `h ∘ F = F_2` and `F^*(D) = div(F_2)`. `F` is étale, so `F^*(D)` is reduced
   197	> (sheet gate Cor 3.4): `F_2` is square-free with zero set `E = {x = 0}`, i.e.
   198	> `F_2 = c·x`, `c ∈ C^*` (units of `C[x,y]` are constants). Then
   199	> `Jac F = -c·∂F_1/∂y ∈ C^*`, so `∂F_1/∂y = λ ∈ C^*` and
   200	> `F_1 = λ y + g(x)`. Then `F = (λ y + g(x), c x)` is an automorphism —
   201	> contradicting noninvertibility. ∎
   202	
