   478	## 7. The cuspidal horn: Lin–Zaidenberg, CUSP-KILL, and the `pi_1` cage
   479	
   480	Case **(A)** — every singular point of `A_F` unibranch — collapses to one curve
   481	up to a target automorphism, and then to a covering-space question.
   482	
   483	> **PROPOSITION 7.1.** In case (A), `A_F` is homeomorphic to `C`, hence by the
   484	> **Lin–Zaidenberg** theorem there is `α ∈ Aut(A^2)` with
   485	> `α(A_F) = {x^p = y^q}`, `gcd(p,q) = 1`; SMOOTH-KILL forces `p, q >= 2`.
   486	> Moreover `s = 1`, `a_p = 1`, `nu = 0`, `K_p = a - 1` (Prop. 6.1 and `(L)`).
   487	>
   488	> *Proof.* `eta : D~ ≅ A^1 -> D` (Lemma A) is a proper morphism, bijective
   489	> because every point of `D` — smooth or singular — is unibranch. A proper
   490	> continuous bijection is a homeomorphism, so `D` is a topologically embedded
   491	> line. Lin–Zaidenberg (Invent. Math. 68 (1982) 1–17: an irreducible plane
   492	> affine curve homeomorphic to `C` is `Aut(C^2)`-equivalent to `{x^p = y^q}`)
   493	> applies. `s = 1` because `{x^p=y^q}` with `p,q >= 2` has exactly one singular
   494	> point. ∎
   495	
   496	Write `G_{p,q} := pi_1(C^2 \ {x^p=y^q}) = <α, β | α^p = β^q>` (the curve is a
   497	cone over the `(p,q)` torus knot, so the complement deformation retracts to
   498	`S^3 \ K_{p,q}`); `Z := Z(G_{p,q}) = <z>`, `z = α^p = β^q`, and
   499	`G_{p,q}/Z ≅ Z/p * Z/q` with trivial centre. `F` is proper and étale over
   500	`A^2 \ D`, so
   501	
   502	```text
   503	(7.1)  F : C^2 \ E  -->  C^2 \ D ,  E := F^{-1}(D),  finite etale of degree N,
   504	       H := pi_1(C^2 \ E)  <=  G_{p,q}  of index N.
   505	```
   506	
   507	`D_0 = D \ {p} ≅ C^*`, so `E_0 := F^{-1}(D_0) -> C^*` is an `a`-sheeted
   508	covering; let `j` be its number of connected components, so `j <= a`, and `E`
   509	has exactly `j` irreducible components (`a_p = 1` puts a single, unibranch point
   510	of `E` over `p`, so at most one component of `E_0` acquires it).
   511	
   512	> **THEOREM CUSP-KILL.** In case (A), if `E` is irreducible (equivalently
   513	> `j = 1`; in particular whenever `a = 1`) then `F` is an automorphism —
   514	> contradiction. Hence `j >= 2` and `a >= 2`.
   515	>
   516	> *Proof.* `j = 1`: `E_0` is a connected `a`-sheeted cover of `C^*`, so
   517	> `E_0 ≅ C^*`; `E_0` is smooth (`F` étale over the smooth `D_0`); `E = E_0 ∪
   518	> {y_0}` with `(E,y_0) ≅ (D,p)` analytically (`F` a local biholomorphism), hence
   519	> unibranch and singular. So `E~ = C^* ∪ {1 place} ≅ A^1` (affine, so not
   520	> `P^1`), the normalization of `E` is bijective, and `E` is homeomorphic to `C`.
   521	> Lin–Zaidenberg again: `E ≅ {x^{p'} = y^{q'}}`, and the analytic type of its
   522	> unique singular point identifies `{p',q'} = {p,q}`. Hence `H ≅ G_{p,q}`.
