   526	> nonelementary (`p,q >= 2`, `gcd(p,q) = 1` excludes `Z/2 * Z/2`), so the
   527	> centralizer of its finite-index subgroup `Delta` is trivial; hence
   528	> `Z(H) = Z_H` and `Delta ≅ H/Z(H) ≅ Z/p * Z/q`. Rational Euler characteristic
   529	> is multiplicative in finite index: `chi(Delta) = M·(1/p + 1/q - 1)` and also
   530	> `= 1/p + 1/q - 1 ≠ 0`, so `M = 1`, i.e. `HZ = G`. `Z` central then makes
   531	> `H ◁ G` with `G/H ≅ Z/Z_H` cyclic of order `N`: the covering (7.1) is Galois,
   532	> so `C(x,y)/C(F_1,F_2)` is a Galois extension. By **Campbell** (Math. Ann. 205
   533	> (1973) 243–248) a Keller map with Galois field extension is invertible. ∎
