   546	   `E_2=c_2 Z eta^2`, `D_2=c_1 Z eta^3` (so `Z D_2^2 = mu E_2^3`);
   547	   `2c_2 C_2 = Z eta (3 c_1 s + c_5 eta)`; and by Proposition 6.1 either
   548	   `E_1=E_2', D_1=D_2'`, or `deg(D_1-D_2') = deg eta + deg(E_1-E_2')`.
